        "original_id": "959a1042-ece6-5162-b43a-12afb3a8768f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Flexible-fuel vehicles, bi-fuel vehicles, hydrogen vehicles\n- Fuels: Compressed natural gas, liquefied petroleum gas, hydrogen\n- Concepts: Separate fuel tanks, onboard fuel, motive power\n\nFacts:\n- Bi-fuel vehicles store two fuels in separate tanks and run the engine on one fuel at a time.\n- Bi-fuel vehicles can use fuels such as compressed natural gas, liquefied petroleum gas, or hydrogen.\n- Flexible-fuel vehicles are distinguished from bi-fuel vehicles.\n- A hydrogen vehicle is a vehicle that uses hydrogen as its onboard fuel for motive power.",
